A||||25||ChadMan||Just test drove an MR2||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||05-09-2000||12:47 PM||||A girl here at work is selling a black '91 MR2 (non-turbo) and a coworker asked me to look it over and drive it and tell him what I thought, so I did.<P>I'd never driven an MR2 before, and to be honest, I was a little afraid I'd come back soured on Fieros.  Nope!  It drove like the world's nicest Corolla.  It supposedly makes 135 hp, but my 86 SE would have smoked that MR2, no contest.  I was expecting some punch above 4K like a VTEC Honda, but all I got was valvetrain noise and gentle acceleration.  The steering/handling was great, but brakes and ride quality were no better than my 88 Coupe.  The clutch felt rubbery and spongy.  And the tiny paint chips that were starting to rust sealed the deal.  Sorry, no MR2 for this guy - though I did recommend it to my buddy because the car seemed was mechanically sound.<P>I feel so much better now.  It's great to know the grass is greenest right here where we are.  Viva la Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||05-09-2000||01:23 PM||||YOu sure it was a 91? The new body style. Hate to burst your bubble, but sadly, the non-turbo will take your SE no hands down. Had one. Could out accelerate, outhandle, and otherwise out perform my 87 GT. It didn't have the rumble though. Sounded like a Honda.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroGTGirl||05-09-2000||02:13 PM||||I have to say, 87PegasusGT, I love the rumble of my Fiero.  whenever I go see my mother she says it sounds like a tractor!LOL<P>I don't really think it is quite that loud..But that is what she thinks...||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||05-09-2000||02:23 PM||||I'm positive it was a '91 (the Ferrari 308-looking kind).  This MR2 simply doesn't have the balls my 86 SE (4-sp, no power goodies) had.  This MR2 might outhandle and outbrake the SE, but in a straight line, no contest - the Toyota would sniff Fiero fumes.  Matter of fact, I think my buddy's '83 944 would also whoop this MR2.<P>Maybe your MR2 was an especially quick one?  Maybe my coworker's MR2 has a clogged cat or something?  Maybe I'm a total dumba$$ for selling my SE (no maybes there)?  Who knows?<P>And I think we can all agree the V6 rumble is like music.  I was stuck in stop-and-go behind a V6 Fiero this morning and I turned off my radio so I could hear his car better!||||reg||1
Z||000004||87PegasusGT||05-09-2000||03:53 PM||||LOL Sounds like me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Yes you drove a 91, but it must have been having problems. I smoked my share of 5.0 Stangs with the MR2 but have not gotten any V8 kills with my Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||05-09-2000||04:39 PM||||ChadMan... Yes you are a dumbass for selling your SE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  jk  you did it for good reasons, but that was a very pretty car, whish I had had the money at the time... then I could be enjoying your SE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||05-09-2000||05:10 PM||||A 91 non-turbo Toyota MR2 will go 0-60 in 8.5 seconds and do the 1/4 in 16.3 seconds. An 86 GT will go 0-60 in 7.5 seconds and do the 1/4 in 16 seconds flat. Those are the facts no ifs, ands, or buts. Those are the specifications for stock vehicles.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||87PegasusGT||05-09-2000||06:12 PM||||hmmm... maybe its my GT thats running poorly...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Homicidal||05-09-2000||06:16 PM||||Viva EL FIERO.  It's not called La Fiera.<P>That would be for FIEROGTGIRL.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||05-09-2000||06:32 PM||||I don't know why but automobile magazine has the 87 fiero GT listed as 0-60 in 8.5 seconds and the ¼ mile in 17 seconds. The specifications for the 86 fiero GT came from Car and Driver magazine.||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||05-09-2000||08:05 PM||||In February of 86 CD got the following stats:<P>0-60: 7.5 sec.<BR>1/4 mile: 15.9 @ 85 mph<BR>That was for an 85 GT.<P>In April of 88 CD got the following:<P>0-60: 7.9 sec.<BR>1/4 mile:16.1 @ 82.0 mph<BR>88 Formula!<P>The only difference?<BR>In 85 the 4 speed had a 3.65 axle. The 88 had the 5 spd with a 3.61...I didn't think that it would have such a difference but it would appear that according to the data in Witzenburg's book the 85 was the fastest.<P>That being said it would be noteworthy to include MotorTrends figures for the 85 GT as well...8.5 seconds to 60, 16.2 seconds @83.8 mph. <BR>Conclusion - Magazines get different figures depending on the car and the driver. An engine with 10,000 miles will always be better than the fresh engine with less than 3. So to smoke a high reving non-turbo MR-2 with a GT? Shouldn't be a problem, unless you got a Fiero that is tired. <P>Hope this sheds some light!||||reg||1
Z||000011||RobertVol||05-10-2000||09:07 AM||||Also remember that the engine in the 88's had a slight downgrade in power...some Stupid CAFE restriction!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||sid1200||05-12-2000||02:12 AM||||Actually there was no actual downgrade in engine power for 88,<BR>the listed number was reduced to 135, due to increasing sound restricions, thus power was calculated at a lower RPM in 88.  however different sources in GM often still quote 140 for the 88 as well, since there was no real loss.||||reg||1
Z||000013||ChadMan||05-12-2000||08:32 AM||||Sorry, Homicidal!  That's what I get for taking French instead of Spanish in high school!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||05-12-2000||09:50 AM||||Since "Fiero" is a proper noun, it would remain "Fiero" (not "Fiera") no matter what the gender.  You are correct about the "el".  Lots of nouns don't change with gender.  La casa/El caso.  Nope.  Always casa.  Been a long time since I took Spanish in HS.  (Graduated in '85.)  I don't remember a whole lot, but maybe enough to get me by.  Only problem is most of the words I can remember would only get me in a fight! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tom88gt||05-12-2000||12:36 PM||||I raced a bunch of 2nd generation MR2s at a big SCCA event in Feb.  They all kicked my ass.  It's about the same hp but lighter.  Plus several years newer, in other words, probably a more refined suspension.  <P>That said, none are new and upkeep and maintenance has a big impact on current power output and handling.  How tired is the engine and how worn out are trhe shocks and springs?<P>Granted, the MR2 is a smoother looking car and certainly more refined in the details and ergonomics.  But my car will never rust and I'm looking to eventually settle in South Florida.  No MR2 is going to look good when the body starts rusting out.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Greg Piet||05-12-2000||03:39 PM||||Since we are discussing mister two's here, What year did the body style change over...<P>Reason being:<BR>There is a "second gen" body style in my class.  My class is limited to 92 and older mr2's naturally aspirated.<BR>The mister killed all the other cars in my class by at least 7 seconds with 2nd place getting a time of 62 seconds.   He was using DOT legal racing tires, but I couldnt see a 7 sec gain with tires alone.  <P>My Fiero expressed to me how humiliated it was and told me it wanted DOT racing tires because it didnt want to be beaten by a MR2.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||87PegasusGT||05-12-2000||03:52 PM||||91 was the 1st of the new breed. Slower time table or not, I have yet to beat a 2nd Gen MR2 with my old 87GT. The MR2 I had only had 30K less miles but it was definitely faster than both my 85 and 87 Gt ?!?!?! Go figure...Doesn't make sense.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Homicidal||05-12-2000||04:41 PM||||Very rarely do the nouns change, as do the pro-nouns.  El and La conform to what the word ends with.<P>Unlike German, which you have NO idea what the pro-noun would be: Die, Das, Den, Der, etc..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||87PegasusGT||05-12-2000||06:18 PM||||Dah.<BR>Muchas Gracias por la informacion.<BR>Bete'.<BR>Nemo de veritas.<BR>Who the heck cares...This ain't languages...||||reg||1
Z||000020||Eric||05-12-2000||08:38 PM||||You autoXers need to stop kicking your car in the butt and start kicking yourself in the butt.  I'm new to the sport too, so I'm not the greatest driver in the world.  But you have to take my word for it, Fieros, in the right hands, can and do beat MR2s on the track.  The 88s, with the proper suspension tuning and tires, can run very fast.  Last Sunday I went to an autoX school.  There was an instructor for every four students.  My instructor drove the balls off my car.  His time (just one run) was so fast that I, even with a year of driving this car, could not approach by damn sight!  The most incredible thing was the fact that he got in and drove cold with very little experience in a mid engine car and almost none in a Fiero.  He also had an extra 170lbs to carry around the track in the passenger's seat.  He said the 88s are some of the best cars ever for an exersise such as autocross.||||reg||1
Z||000021||terryk||05-13-2000||12:54 AM||||Which brings us to Gaelic, the most dangerous of all languages.....<P>Dang, what were we talking about?||||reg||5
Z||000022||Greg Piet||05-13-2000||06:49 AM||||Although I am a rookie in the autocross world, I put a fair amount of the reason why I lose to my own driving, but lets get real. Using "normal" tires that will last for 35-50k miles on the road is a completely different story that using a set of DOT legal racing tires that will get 10k miles if you are very lucky.<P>I had some extremely experienced race car drivers ride with me (ex Fiero racers and some current) to tell me where I was screwing up.  I was told I was driving darn near perfect (shifting times, my lines on the track, my braking times, etc...)except for one turn which I already knew I was screwing up.  They also told me I was pushing the car about as hard as I could w/o getting completely out of control (meaning I was pushing my tires to their limit).<P>Now that I've tried to defend my own ego, I was asking about the misters because of the extreme time differential.  There was a guy who has been racing for darn near 30 years and kicks butt, and he even lost in his miata  to the mister with DOT racing tires by 7 seconds.  The classes are to compare "equal" cars and I wanted to make sure that second gen was a "equal" car according to the rulebook.    <P>    ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Black88GT||05-14-2000||12:18 PM||||   After I got into an accident with my yellow formula, I considered an MR2.  First I drove a '91 N/A....yawn.  It cornered well and had nice brakes, but it was like driving a Tercel.  And for the money they go for, definitely not worth it.  I then test drove a '92 Turbo.  Sweet car, the noise of the turbo spooling up could take some getting used to though over the nice hum of the Fiero V6. The only problem was it needed a turbo rebuild and the price was around $10k (what they go for).  I could put half that money into a fiero and blow the doors off a MR2 turbo.  I think the MkII's have nicer interiors, but there brakes are about equal to the '88 brakes, oh and I didn't like how close the pedals were to eachother. The clutch felt weird too, it was hard to drive it when I first started off. The rear view is about the same on a fastback GT.  The suspension is a little nicer on them over '88 Fiero's, way better then 84-87s without a doubt. Also, I didnt like the power steering on the MkII.  One thing that I must say impressed me was the shifting on them.  It is way smoother then a Fiero's getrag (note I have driven with a fresh getrag and clutch in my old formula) hands down. <BR>   The money issue is important too. For that MR2 my insurance would be double what I am paying now for my GT!! And for the money I bought my '88 GT t-top for, I am very satisfied! I am planning on a 3.2 soon and some other mods, around 215 Hp, I could easily take a turbo MR2 with that, and I haven't even spent 4,000 bucks (car included)....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 05-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000024||Haze_Performance||05-16-2000||02:13 AM||||I raced a VERY cute girl today in a MR2 Turbo(black in color) I SMOKED HER!!!!! IT WASNT EVEN CLOSE!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>ok, It was in my Mustang NOT the Fiero   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> . But a win is a win right?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000025||87PegasusGT||05-16-2000||01:16 PM||||What year is your Stang? Is it stock. Because I smoked several 5.0s with a non turbo. It was off the line though. ||||reg||1
